  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict, immediate reporting (24h for serious, 5 business days for others) and customer notice. S2 sets a 5% failure limit with a 12-month remediation window allowing continued sales under safeguards, and per-model results to customers/regulators but not public. S3 requires new units to have shut-off after 18 months (weakened) and retrofits within 6 years. S4 requires built-in suppression after 3 years. S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents/100k with 24h notice, but no serious-injury clause."
